  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NDICI AFRICA/2024/Enhancing Food Security and Resilience of Rural Communities in Sudan (EFSR Project)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall objective:&lt;/strong&gt; To contribute to sustainable livelihoods and food security in rural communities most affected by food insecurity, climate change and conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective/Outcome 1:&lt;/strong&gt; Sustainably increase productivity and profitability of smallholder agriculture and livestock nutritious short value chains using agro ecological practices adapted to climate change&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 1.1:&lt;/strong&gt; Smallholder farmers (with focus on women and youth) in nutritious value chains organised, trained and informed. &lt;strong&gt;Output 1.2:&lt;/strong&gt; Agricultural and livestock input availability and access and outreach to farmers enhanced. &lt;strong&gt;Output 1.3:&lt;/strong&gt; knowledge and skills provided to young people on business opportunities along priority agricultural and livestock value chains.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific Objective/Outcome 2:&lt;/strong&gt; Increase sustainable and decent jobs opportunities for both genders within the youth, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), people with disabilities (PwD), in rural and food insecure areas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 2.1:&lt;/strong&gt; Climate-resilient infrastructure rehabilitated or constructed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 2.2:&lt;/strong&gt; Decent job opportunities through cash for work created.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 2.3:&lt;/strong&gt; Emergency cash-based support for food security provided to acutely food insecure target groups.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
